      "side": 1,
      "message": "A lot of the logic is about checking whether this is a pattern filter or an address filter, and currently it\u0027s done by checking whether the handle maps to a None or some address.\n\nHow about never insert the pattern handle to `monitor_handle_map` instead? This way we can check:\n`if monitor_handle \u003d\u003d handle` --\u003e pattern filter\n`else if monitor_handle_map.contains_key(handle)` --\u003e address filter\n`else` --\u003e bad handle\n\nHopefully that can simplify a lot of the logic? e.g. if it\u0027s an address filter, we skip the check whether it\u0027s already added to the handle_map.\n\nIf you decide to implement this, the value of the map can directly be the address, and not `Option\u003cAddress\u003e`.\nAlso, you must only assign the pattern monitor handle to `scanner.monitor_handle` and not assign the address monitor handle.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1853,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 1853,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "3cf6d57bc6ea29fed1ad75d8d6c3d137aedaad80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
